window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>A trans boy enters a throw-down battle for the title of homecoming king with the boy he dumped last summer in ZR Ellor's contemporary YA debut. </b></p> <p>Jeremy Harkiss, cheer captain and student body president, won’t let coming out as a transgender boy ruin his senior year. Instead of bowing to the bigots and outdated school administration, Jeremy decides to make some noise - and how better than by challenging his all-star ex-boyfriend, Lukas, for the title of homecoming king? </p> <p>Lukas Rivers, football star and head of the Homecoming Committee, is just trying to find order in his life after his older brother’s funeral and the loss of his long-term girlfriend - who turned out to be a boy. But when Jeremy threatens to break his heart and steal his crown, Lukas kick starts a plot to sabotage Jeremy’s campaign. </p> <p>When both boys take their rivalry too far, the dance is on the verge of being canceled. To save homecoming, they’ll have to face the hurt they’re both hiding - and the lingering butterflies they can’t deny. </p> <p><b>A Macmillan Audio production from Roaring Brook Press </b></p>"; 
